This is the result of a source dive to fully understand the little
known monster digestion attack instadeath. It is little known because
it usually only happens at very high AC (AC > 0 , AC -> +10).

On file You.h, line 296, it is defined:
<code>
 unsigned uswldtim;               /* time you have been swallowed */
</code>
I believe this comment is wrong and should be something like
"Time left to be relesased" or "Number of turns to be swallowed"
Actually it is the number of attacks you will suffer while
engulfed, so it does not translate directly to the number of turns,
since the monster may be slow or fast.

Considering the digestion attack, all action happens on mhitu.c,
on function gulpmu: lines 1620-1810
<code>
gulpmu(mtmp, mattk)/*monster swallows you, or damage if u.uswallow*/
</code>

The damage dealt on engulf (or while engulfed) attacks is usually
calculated at the beginning of the function, at line 1628:
<code>
int     tmp = d((int)mattk->damn, (int)mattk->damd);
</code>

However, exceptions may occur: you may be invulerable to that kind
of attack (tmp = 0), or you may get an instadeath (tmp = u.uhp ).

For the purpose of this post, which is to describe digestion
instadeath, I will only consider the engulf case of Digestion,
defined on Monattk.h, line 63 as:
<code>
#define AD_DGST	26	/* digests opponent (trapper, etc.) */
</code>
The only 3 monsters with that attack are lurkers above, trappers
and purple worms.
Trappers have level 12 and speed 3
Lurkers above have level 10 and speed 3
Purple worms have level 15 and speed 9

The level matters for the uswldtim calculation, and speed is not
involved on that, but it matters since uswldtim decreases at each
attack from the engulfing monster.
For the worst scenario, then, it only matters the purple worm.
As a matter of fact, I did this source dive after a purple worm
instadeath on a very advanced monk with AC = +10; HP 135/148 -> 0 in
one turn (engulfed on turn x, died on turn x+1).

Rigth next to the initial damage calculation, there is a
<code>if (!u.uswallow) {	/* swallows you */</code>
from lines 1633 to 1693.
So, if you were not swallowed before, you are now and this 'if'
takes care of that.
Appart from accounting for steeds, traps, etc, the relevant part is
at the end of the if, where uswldtim is calculated.

<code>
u.uswallow = 1;
/* u.uswldtim always set > 1 */
tim_tmp = 25 - (int)mtmp->m_lev;
if (tim_tmp > 0) tim_tmp = rnd(tim_tmp) / 2;
else if (tim_tmp < 0) tim_tmp = -(rnd(-tim_tmp) / 2);
tim_tmp += -u.uac + 10;
u.uswldtim = (unsigned)((tim_tmp < 2) ? 2 : tim_tmp);
swallowed(1);
</code>

So, for m_lev = 15, we have
tim_tmp = 25 - 15 = 10
tim_tmp > 0
tim_tmp = rnd(10) / 2 = [ 1 ; 10 ] / 2 = [ 0 ; 5 ]

Considering AC = 10
tim_tmp += -u.uac + 10 => tim_tmp = [ 0 ; 5 ];

uswldtim = Max(2, tim_tmp) = [2 ; 5]

So, after being engulfed by a purple w at AC = 10, the hero will be
expelled after 2, 3, 4 or 5 digestion attacks.
However, the gulpmu is not finished, and after the 'if' we have:
if (u.uswldtim > 0) u.uswldtim -= 1;

This means that after the engulf the hero has 1, 2, 3 or 4 monster
attacks until total digestion.

Next, there is a switch to pick the kind of engulf attack. Since
we only care for AD_DGST, we only look at lines 1700-1714.

<code>
case AD_DGST:
    if (Slow_digestion) {
	/* Messages are handled below */
 	u.uswldtim = 0;
 	tmp = 0;
     } else if (u.uswldtim == 0) {
 	pline("%s totally digests you!", Monnam(mtmp));
 	tmp = u.uhp;
 	if (Half_physical_damage) tmp *= 2; /* sorry */
     } else {
 	pline("%s%s digests you!", Monnam(mtmp),
 	      (u.uswldtim == 2) ? " thoroughly" :
 	      (u.uswldtim == 1) ? " utterly" : "");
	exercise(A_STR, FALSE);
    }
</code>

If the hero has slow digestion, the damage is set to 0 and uswldtim
is set to 0 so (s)he is expelled at the end of gulpmu.

Else, if uswldtim == 0, we get the instadeath: tmp (the damage of
the engulf attack) is set to the hero's HP. If the hero has half
physical damage, double that, because at the end of gulpmu damage
will be halved. This gives a message like "The purple worm totally
digests you!"

Else, uswldtim > 0 and we only get a warning message and abuse
strength. At this point, if you get a "The purple worm utterly
digests you!" and you're not sure of killing the monster on a single
turn, use that /oDigging!


